WEBVTT

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.240
I wanted to feel the wind...

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.320
A faster wind than any I could feel in this world.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:29.800
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.460
Always go

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.880
On my own

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.100
Always go

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:48.730
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:56.110
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:02.200
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:11.130
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.670
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:24.310
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:30.360
All we have left is the future

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:36.780
Please become our reason to continue living

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:43.490
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.520
How much can you narrow down the time frame?

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.930
I'm sorry.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.270
All Pitz knows is that it'll be tonight.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.480
But he's sure it'll be somewhere in this area...

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.280
Tonight, huh?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.320
Be careful.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.700
Remember that Akari was kidnapped last time.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.780
It wasn't a big deal...

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.700
It most certainly was a big deal!

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.710
It was my fault.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.420
It's nothing you should worry about, Teppei.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.880
I should have been with you.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.130
Everyone, I'm sorry that I can't assist you at a time like this.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.930
We're a team. We cover for each other.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:42.680
That's right.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:48.520
But I'm the only one not helping the team, again.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.600
Teppei...

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.810
For a combat unit,

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.610
the most important thing is that everyone knows their own capabilities.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.530
Right now, you need to be focusing on your

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.200
tests with the Livlaster at Tanegashima.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.580
If it goes well, the Midsummer's Knights will find themselves stronger than ever.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.370
We're counting on you, Teppei.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.700
It's just like the rumors say...

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.660
What rumors?

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.830
That there's a woman who rides her bike like it was made of wind.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.210
Do you really think you're unbeatable?

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.170
Only because I am.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.630
What's your name?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:00.880
Lin.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.930
Where do you go to school?

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:04.930
I don't.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.760
You've got a pretty nice machine here.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:08.600
Are you rich?

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.650
This is some good wind.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:22.320
On the
Windy Planet

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.410
Seaside University

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.410
Hey, Dr. Marimura...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.370
Who is this "Robin" that's funding our research project?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.250
You really want to know?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.590
Everyone's asking about it.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.050
Ban...

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:45.130
Until a few years ago, I was researching the use of transcranial magnetic stimulation

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:49.510
to control the dreams of sleeping research subjects.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.430
A system that would let you manipulate your dreams?

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.900
If that really worked, it would have any number of applications

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.860
in psychiatry and clinical psychology.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:04.360
Robin was the one who took an interest in the research and offered to fund it.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:10.990
But I don't actually know if Robin is even a single person!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.370
But now I understand.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:19.340
This project's name, "Install," refers to installing dreams.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:20.920
No.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.050
That isn't what it means.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.180
Hey, you're here, Mao.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.220
Oh, Lin...

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:30.930
Welcome.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:35.180
Hey, you can't speak to Dr. Marimura like that!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.310
Relax... She's a friend.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.520
What brings you here today?

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.730
Looking for your allowance?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.280
I'm glad we're on the same page.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.820
Yeah.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.280
I want a faster machine...

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.800
Come down, Pitz.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:06.800
Let's go.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.510
Sorry!

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.970
Wait a second... My pendant got stuck.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.240
I got it.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:33.700
Yeah.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.790
Ah, such innocence.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.050
Teppei...

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.560
I feel pretty bad about what I said to him.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.480
I didn't know he thought it was such a big deal.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.390
From now on, we should be more careful.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.230
Roger.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:08.820
But personally, I'm kind of glad that Teppei felt bad not being here.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.860
Yeah.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.660
She's been completely hypnotized.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.160
Why is she so important to you?

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:25.800
Her security is of the utmost importance to this project's future.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:27.840
Now, Lin...

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:35.510
You are in a world deep within your heart, where your soul is free.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.270
How do you feel about your daily life?

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.020
I love the speed of my machine.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.980
I want to go faster.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.740
That's right, Lin.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:53.030
The machine gives you freedom.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:57.030
But doesn't anything bother you about how you're living right now?

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:03.790
Not as long as the real me is somewhere else...

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.790
The real you?

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.670
That's an interesting thing to say.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.010
What is the real you?

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.090
It's...

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.720
Who are you?!

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.430
This place is off-limits to non-personnel!

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.270
Get out of there!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.000
I'll contact security!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.870
Wait...

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.210
Look at the variance in her brain waves...

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.840
Can you believe that this is the same person?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.220
Amazing...

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.680
Dr. Marimura?

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:03.350
You are also Designer's Children, aren't you?

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.600
What are you saying, Doctor?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.480
We are the Planetary Gears.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.400
We reveal the world's dreams.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.590
I knew he'd be here.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.710
Manatsu Daichi?

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.430
Should we eliminate him here?

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:42.890
He's the Earthling who drove Albion crazy?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.390
I'd like to play with him a bit.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.560
Do as you like.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.320
But he's a Neoteny.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.780
Don't forget that.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.370
They look so happy, swimming around in there.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Eyecatch

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.800
They look so happy, swimming around in there.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:19.680
Their own ignorance is certainly the only thing that lets them be that way.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.310
Well, there are some things you can be happier not knowing.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.310
But all living things must die.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.640
They're all the same.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.400
They aren't the same.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.650
Having to die means your existence is incomplete.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:40.240
How can you people possibly believe that
immortality is necessary to be a true human?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.370
Because it's true...

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.870
You people aren't actually human.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.160
And that's why your death is inevitable.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:52.540
Hey, how do you feel about the fact that you will one day die?

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:57.340
Don't you feel pathetic, only living for such a short amount of time?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:04.430
Someone once told me that when you die,
you should do it with a smile.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.470
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:10.520
All creatures like you <i>can</i> do is smile as you die.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.690
No...

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.940
I don't think that's what he meant.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.280
Stop quibbling, Neoteny.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.550
Where'd he go?

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.090
When did you...

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.130
You're fast.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.850
I was on the track team.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.560
Is that the Tanegashima Livlaster?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.310
Slowly raise your hands, and give me your gun.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.400
We'll finish this later, Earthling.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.080
This machine is fast, right?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.040
Yeah...

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.160
Faster than anything you've ever ridden.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.250
You do know how it works, don't you, Liban?

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.130
Yeah.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.630
I'll settle things with that Neoteny.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.420
Abreaction!

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.560
MM bus signal detected!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.060
I've located the epicenter of the Machine Goodfellow's activation area.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.190
This is bad...

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.940
It's underwater!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.160
Hana said it would appear in this area...

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.570
It will be near me.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:52.910
I'm sure she'll come to finish our fight!

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.460
She?

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.920
You made contact with her?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.250
All right.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.380
I believe in you, Captain.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.580
Captain, ready?

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:38.670
Go ahead.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.630
Earth Engine Ordinary, launch!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.600
I knew she'd come.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.310
Let's fight, Earthling!

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.240
An underwater fight?

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:17.870
She's fast!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:31.510
You were a fool to dive into the sea,
former track athlete!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.970
Captain, there's no time!

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:36.680
I know!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:42.770
What?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.730
This is the end!

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.330
I win.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:01.920
I lost her.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.270
Yes...

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.020
This is it.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:20.230
This is the real me...

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.940
And this is my real speed!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.570
AEO confirmed.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.400
A Kill-T-Gang Type-4!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.910
Manifestation area lies within
Defensive Zone 1, Omicron sector!

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.450
Area Impactors are initiating interception!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.370
You let her escape, Daichi...

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.500
Call off Teppei's test!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.880
No, I'm going up.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.750
What are you going to do, Teppei?

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:51.720
The <i>Tenkaido</i> has an Impactor ready to go that can expand with this machine.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.510
That's a modified development prototype.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:58.640
And how did you even know about it?

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.680
Did Akari tell you?!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:01.390
Stop!

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:07.190
You haven't even flown the <i>Aramusha</i> once since it was re-outfitted!

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.110
This isn't the <i>Aramusha</i> anymore.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:11.950
It is the Nebula Engine Ordinary.

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.410
I've instructed him in usage of its basic weaponry.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.160
I just hadn't gotten around to asking permission yet.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:19.490
Science Chief!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.910
Teppei can do this!

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.000
Let me go, Commander.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:27.750
If my captain let her escape, I have to do it.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.050
We're a team, so we cover for each other!

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.590
Commander!

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.550
Daichi, you're listening, right?

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:39.220
You are the captain!

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.520
What should we do?

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:44.020
Give me the order, Captain.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.480
Do it, Teppei.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.690
Roger, Captain.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.570
Governor Yomatsuri...

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:57.530
I'm sending up the Nebula.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.830
Are you serious?

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.120
Understood.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:04.290
Mia...

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.170
Right!

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.580
Initiating expansion sequence.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:14.420
The <i>Regenbogen</i> is purging the Nebula Engine!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.440
The Nebula Engine's energy is charging!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:59.360
This light... Orgone energy?

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.420
Liban?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.630
A Livlaster?

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:17.170
Too slow!

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.680
You're too slow, Neoteny!

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:36.980
She disappeared?

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.170
You're too slow to keep up with me.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.630
This speed...

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.460
It's too fast to follow with the naked eye.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.760
Feel it...

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.100
The flow of the Orgone energy.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.020
It's over,

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.940
second Neoteny!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.320
There!

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.530
This light...

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.530
What is it?

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:08.910
The Nebula Engine has successfully repelled the Kill-T-Gang Type-4.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.080
You were correct.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:16.670
They'll make a great team.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.340
We did it!

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.510
He's taken it back again...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.060
There was another Neoteny.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.230
What?

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:40.110
But what is that energy the Livlaster emits?

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:44.360
It felt like a wonderful wind...

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:48.320
What are you saying?

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.040
Wake up, Dr. Marimura!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.250
Oh, good...

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.420
Who were they?

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:01.800
Anyway, let's talk to the police.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:02.880
Wait.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.260
There's no need for that...

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.590
There's no need for that.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.510
Doctor...

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:32.330
Welcome back, Miss Mao.

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:36.040
You were waiting for me?

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.290
I'm home, Setsuna.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:55.020
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:55.020 --> 00:23:00.480
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.320
aren't always good things

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:12.990
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:22.460
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:30.720
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:36.680
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:42.520
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:45.610
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:53.780
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:57.200
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:03.330
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:17.720
Only two unawakened Designer's Children remain.

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:21.350
We've followed one of them to a
medical equipment manufacturer.

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:25.480
But Hana says her premonition isn't as clear as usual.

00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:29.230
Huh? An enemy Machine Goodfellow isn't going to activate?

00:24:29.230 --> 00:24:30.610
What do you mean?

00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:33.860
Next time, on episode 11 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:33.860 --> 00:24:35.450
Through the Window of Setsuna.

00:24:33.860 --> 00:24:35.450
Through the Window of Setsuna

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:38.370
Earth Engine, scramble!
